## Step 3: Modifying your application

Now that your service is running in OpenShift, you'll want to make a
change and deploy the new version.  First, let's back to our
application repo in gitea.

We want to change the "Hello World" message to "Bonjour Monde".  The
code for displaying "Hello World" is found in `app.py`.  Click on
`app.py` to view the code.

Gitea has a nice built-in web-based editor you can use to make your
change.  Click on the pencil icon near the top right of your code
window to bring up the editor.  Now go to line 8 of the python program
and make the necessary change as below.

Once you've edited your code, you need to commit this change back into
gitea's git repo.  Scroll down to find the green `Commit Changes`
button, and click on that.

Now that you've changed your code in gitea, switch back to your
project on OpenShift.  Bring up the sidebar on the right again, and
find the `Start Build` button.  Clicking on that should start a new
build, where it will pull your code from git and create a new
container image.  Once built, it will automatically deploy the new
version, and clicking on the route should bring up `Bonjour Monde` in
your browser.

